{"purpose":"Record that the acronym \"EKA\" collides with an unrelated open-source project, and that the collision is recorded separately and does NOT block the EKA v2 program.","content":"The OSS project `EKA-Community/eka` uses \"EKA\" for \"Executable Knowledge Architecture\" and operates in the knowledge-graph space. It is unrelated to this EKA (the engineering-knowledge system: eka-standard, eka-core, eka-cli, eka-mcp). The collision is a naming/discovery concern (search results, package registries, documentation), not a technical dependency.","investigationSummary":"Identified during EKA v2 planning. Checked: no technical dependency and no shared artifact; the collision is name-only and sits in a different problem space (knowledge graphs vs engineering knowledge). Impact is limited to discoverability and potential user confusion.","conclusion":"Recorded as a separate finding. Decision: the acronym collision does NOT block EKA v2. Any mitigation (renaming, disambiguation docs, registry namespacing) is a separate future decision outside this plan."}